# postN — Cursor Rules

## Reference Codebase
You have access to the open-source Postiz social media scheduler at ./_reference/
Use it to study patterns but NEVER copy code directly. Write fresh implementations.

## Key reference paths:
- OAuth + social providers: _reference/libraries/nestjs-libraries/src/integrations/social/
- Database schema: _reference/prisma/schema.prisma
- Job scheduling: _reference/libraries/nestjs-libraries/src/bull-mq-transport/
- Post creation: _reference/apps/backend/src/api/routes/posts/
- Frontend components: _reference/apps/frontend/src/components/

## Our stack:
- Product: postN
- Frontend: Next.js App Router + Tailwind
- Backend: NestJS + Prisma + PostgreSQL
- Queue: Redis + BullMQ
- Media: Cloudflare R2
- Auth: NestJS Google OAuth + JWT cookie (no NextAuth)
- AI: Claude API (Sonnet)
- Payments: Razorpay (after MVP core)

## Patterns to follow:
- Provider abstraction: each social platform implements BaseProvider
- Posts have PostTargets (one per platform) with independent status tracking
- BullMQ delayed jobs for scheduling; store jobId; publish must be idempotent
- NestJS owns all OAuth callbacks on :4000
- Shared types in packages/shared
- Default timezone Asia/Kolkata; store timestamps in UTC
